  "notes": "FAA model shown as 737-800. Drawn from the July 2026 photo of N8555Z (left side). The disc is drawn as a circle on the skin, cut by the crown and the belly as it is in the photo; whether it continues across the belly is not seen. Re-checked 2026-11-15: the fin is the state jets' Heart fin as re-measured on Colorado One (the same fin on every 737), copied with its 'Southwest' title and flag. 'Tennessee One' measured on the July 2026 left photo against the nose and the forward door (1.8-2.8 m back), two weights, a pair of titles per side (the right mirrored: the only photo shows the left), on Colorado One's line under the cockpit windows. The white stripe ahead of the blue tail is a curve, and wider than first drawn: about 0.8 m at the crown narrowing to 0.2 m at the belly (it had been 0.15 m throughout); its edges re-measured on the photo (side-on: the door probes within 0.002 of the 737-800's) and made smooth, as are the disc and its ring.",
  "history": "Previously N922WN and N8620H."
}
